Reference:
Title	Genome-wide microRNA expression profiling in renal cell carcinoma: significant down-regulation of miR-141 and miR-200c
Author	Nakada C, Matsuura K, Tsukamoto Y, Tanigawa M, Yoshimoto T, Narimatsu T, Nguyen L, Hijiya N, Uchida T, Sato F, Mimata H, Seto M, Moriyama M
Journal	J Pathol.
Year	2008
Volume	216
Issue	4
Page	418-427
Pubmed ID	18925646

Protocol:
Name	miRNeasy mini kit
Description	Total RNA was extracted with a miRNeasy mini kit (Qiagen, Valencia, CA, USA) according to the manufacturer&#8217;s instructions.

Name	miRNA labeling and hyridization
Description	100 ng of total RNA was labeled with Cy3 and hybridized with a miRNA labeling and hybridization kit (Agilent Technologies, Santa Clara, CA, USA) according to the manufacturer&#8217;s instructions.

Name	Hybridization
Description	Using a miRNA labeling and hybridization kit (Agilent Technologies), the labeled RNA was hybridized to miRNA 8x15K array (Agilent miRNA array G4470A) at 55&deg;C for 20 hours.

Name	Scanning
Description	The arrays were scanned with a laser confocal scanner (G2565BA, Agilent Technologies) and Agilent Scan Control software ver.7.0.

Name	Feature extraction
Description	The intensities of fluorescence were calculated by Feature extraction software ver.9.5 (Agilent Technologies).<br>Calculating protocol, miRNA-v1_95_May07 (Agilent Technologies).

Name	Normalization
Description	After transformation, specific samples were normalized to one another: 26 samples were normalized against the median of the 6 normal samples. Each measurement for each miRNA in those specific samples was divided by the median of that miRNA&#8217;s measurements in the corresponding control samples.

Name	Transformation
Description	Values in raw data below 0.01 were set to 0.01.

Name	array design
Description	Human mature miRNAs (470 miRNAs) and virus miRNAs (64 miRNAs). Sanger miRBase 9.1.

